'''Branchiostoma''' (brang-ki-os′tọ̄-mä̤), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. βράγχια, gills, + στόμα, mouth: see ''stoma''.]

'''1.''' A genus of leptocardians in which the mouth is surrounded by fringes, which were at one time erroneously supposed to have the func-
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Head of Lancelet (''Branchiostoma'', or ''Amphioxus, lanceolatus''), enlarged.}}}}
{{smaller block|''a'', notochord; ''b'', representatives of fin-rays, or neural spines; ''c'', jointed oral ring; ''d'', filamentary appendages of the mouth; ''e'', ciliated lobes of pharynx; ''f'', ''g'', part of branchial sac; ''h'', ''h'', spinal cord.}}
tions of branchiæ: synonymous with ''Amphioxus''. {{smaller|It represents a special family, ''Branchiostomidæ'', an order ''Pharyngobranchii'' or ''Cirrostomi'', a class ''Leptocardii'', and a superclass ''Acrania'', of vertebrate animals. See these words, and ''Amphioxus''.}}

'''2.''' A genus of myriapods. ''Newport'', 1846.

'''branchiostomatous''' (brang″ki-os-tō′mạ-tus), ''a.'' Same as ''branchiostomous''.

'''branchiostome''' (brang′ki-os-tōm), ''n.'' A member of the genus ''Branchiostoma''; an amphioxus

